package angelica:plugin@1.0.0;

/// Game files the plugin replaces.
///
/// The host checks a replacement against the game's original file before
/// serving it, and serves only formats it can check: font tables (`.fdt`)
/// keep the original's headers and kerning and keep every glyph inside the
/// font's atlas; textures (`.tex`) stay 2D, 3D, or cube as the original
/// is, in a format the game uses, with every mip level inside the file
/// (font textures keep the original's header and size, so only their
/// pixels change); materials (`.mtrl`) fill their size exactly, keep
/// every name, constant, and sampler inside it, and use a shader package
/// of the game's materials; models (`.mdl`) keep every count, offset,
/// range, and index inside the model. When the game then loads the file, it reads
/// the replacement. Files the game loaded before keep what it read until it
/// loads them again; a plugin that replaces files in `start` while the game
/// starts covers everything the game loads.
///
/// Requires `files.replace`. Called from the main instance only.
interface file-replacements {
    use types.{error};

    /// Serves the file at `storage-path` in the plugin's storage whenever
    /// the game loads `game-path`, such as `common/font/AXIS_12.fdt`.
    /// Refused when the game has no such file, the file in storage is
    /// larger than 64 MiB, the format cannot be checked, the check fails,
    /// or another plugin replaces the file.
    replace: func(game-path: string, storage-path: string) -> result<_, error>;

    /// Serves the game's own file again from its next load.
    restore: func(game-path: string) -> result<_, error>;
}
